@@ -47,3 +47,5 @@ Built 2026-11-01 in the voice-recite task ([requirements](/framework/ai/sessions
   - **The place.** `{i, t}` per key (sentence within the bubble, seconds in), kept in memory and in `localStorage` `lew42.recite.places` (newest 200, at most one write a second, always on pause or stop). Alternative: a word index — Kokoro gives no word times, and the highlight already places the word from `t` over the sentence's seconds, so a seconds offset resumes at the same word. Heard to the end: the place is cleared.
   - **Replay calls `stop()`.** One rule for "the owner chose to play this": whatever is queued is dropped, nothing marked played. The alternative (keep the waiting replies and put the bubble first) needs a queue insert and a resume of the old one, and tapping a bubble is already the owner saying "this one, now". Revisit if the owner loses replies this way.
   - **Audio is made again each time** (never kept), sentences before the place are not rendered; back-10 counts them by an estimate of 15 characters a second.
+- **A settled reply reads only what the stream did not (playback-stutter, 2026-11-02).** `partial("")` keeps the stream's chunks as `streamed`; `final(text)` compares sentence by sentence (`unread_tail`, on `norm`) and queues just the tail, re-keying the streamed chunks to the bubble so replay still works. A text that is not an extension of the stream is queued whole behind it, never cutting it off. Rejected: muting barge-in for the first seconds (the owner: much less responsive) and `read()`/`stop()` on a mismatch (that was the restart). The phone's old build did exactly that: its `final()` called `read()`. Alternative that would win: have the server send the settled text before the first stream chunk, so no comparison is needed.
+- **The `words` interrupt lives in `BargeIn` only.** `mode` (`volume`|`words`) is read in `trigger()`: in `words` it skips the immediate `pause("heard")` and pauses after the Whisper check returns real, non-echo, non-phantom text; the chat-mic path (`owner_spoke`) was already text-based. Setting kept in the class (`defaults`, `barge_mode` in localStorage), not in Mic.js SETTINGS, so the dictate plugin work can lift it whole. Alternative: a lower threshold in `volume` (still pauses on a bang). Costs ~`listen_ms` of extra talk-over before a real interruption lands.
